<SiteLayout title="Privacy notice — Retail POS Mobile website" description="Draft privacy notice for the pre-launch Retail POS Mobile website." path="/privacy/" noindex={true}>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy notice</div><span class="eyebrow">Website privacy</span><h1>A draft notice for the initial static website.</h1><div class="draft-banner">Draft for review — not the final public policy.</div><p>This page describes the intended initial website setup. It must be checked against the actual hosting configuration and applicable requirements before public launch.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container content-wrap"><h2>Website data collection</h2><p>The initial site is being built without user accounts, contact forms, newsletter sign-up, or analytics. It does not connect to the POS database and is not intended to receive shop sales, customer, supplier, or ledger data.</p><h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2><p>When deployed, the hosting provider may process technical information such as request metadata for delivery, security, and operations. The final notice must identify the actual provider and link to its applicable privacy information.</p><h2>Cookies and tracking</h2><p>No analytics or advertising tracker is part of the initial site code. This must be rechecked in the final production build and hosting configuration before the statement is treated as final.</p><h2>Contact and requests</h2><p>The website currently has no contact form and does not collect support requests. A verified support channel and a process for privacy questions must be added before pilot access opens.</p><h2>Updates to this notice</h2><p>The notice must be reviewed whenever hosting, analytics, forms, or data collection changes. The final published version should include its effective date and an appropriate contact route.</p></div></section></SiteLayout>
